## Story Description
Edit src/models/database.py to add SQLAlchemy Core table definitions for ingestion_batches and transactions_raw, add source_raw_id to transactions_table, and add four helper functions: create_batch(), insert_raw_transactions() with deduplication, get_queued_raw_rows(), and mark_raw_rows_processed(). All new tables are added to the shared metadata object so they are created in SQLite for local dev and tests.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: src/models/database.py
- Add to metadata: ingestion_batches_table with columns id (Text PK), engagement_id (Text), filename (Text), row_count (Integer), new_rows (Integer), duplicate_rows (Integer), status (Text), uploaded_at (Text), completed_at (Text)
- Add to metadata: transactions_raw_table with columns id (Text PK), engagement_id (Text), batch_id (Text), source_row_hash (Text), pipeline_status (Text), invoice_number (Text), invoice_date (Text), raw_supplier_name (Text), base_amount (Float), raw_data (Text), created_at (Text)
- Add column source_raw_id (Text, nullable=True) to the existing transactions_table definition
- Add function create_batch(engine, engagement_id, filename, row_count) -> str: inserts a row into ingestion_batches with status='processing' and returns the batch id (UUID string)
- Add function insert_raw_transactions(engine, records: list[dict], batch_id: str, engagement_id: str) -> tuple[int, int]: inserts records in chunks of 5000 using INSERT OR IGNORE (SQLite) / INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING (Postgres) on source_row_hash; returns (new_rows_count, duplicate_rows_count)
- Add function get_queued_raw_rows(engine, engagement_id: str, batch_id: str) -> pd.DataFrame: returns all transactions_raw rows with pipeline_status='queued' for the given engagement_id and batch_id
- Add function mark_raw_rows_processed(engine, row_ids: list[str], status: str) -> None: updates pipeline_status for the given ids in transactions_raw
- Add function update_batch_status(engine, batch_id: str, status: str, new_rows: int, duplicate_rows: int) -> None: updates ingestion_batches row with final counts and completed_at timestamp
- Detect Postgres vs SQLite in insert_raw_transactions: check if 'postgresql' in str(engine.url) to choose ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING vs OR IGNORE syntax
- Verify: python -c "from src.models.database import ingestion_batches_table, transactions_raw_table, create_batch, insert_raw_transactions, get_queued_raw_rows, mark_raw_rows_processed, update_batch_status; print('OK')" succeeds

