## Story Description
Edit src/ingestion/ingest.py to add a static method compute_source_row_hash() and a new instance method ingest_to_raw() that writes to transactions_raw instead of transactions. The hash is SHA256 of the full original CSV row dict (sorted keys, JSON-serialised). The existing ingest_to_db() method must remain unchanged so all existing tests continue to pass.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: src/ingestion/ingest.py
- Add import: import hashlib
- Add import at top of file: from src.models.database import create_batch, insert_raw_transactions, update_batch_status
- Add static method Ingestor.compute_source_row_hash(raw_row_dict: dict) -> str: returns hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(raw_row_dict, sort_keys=True, default=str).encode()).hexdigest()
- Add method Ingestor.ingest_to_raw(file_path: str, engine, engagement_id: str, source_system: str = None) -> dict: reads the file, creates a batch via create_batch(), computes source_row_hash for each row using the original raw CSV dict (before column mapping), builds records for transactions_raw with all required fields (id=str(uuid4()), batch_id, engagement_id, source_row_hash, invoice_number, invoice_date, raw_supplier_name, base_amount, raw_data=json.dumps(raw_row), pipeline_status='queued', created_at), calls insert_raw_transactions() in chunks, calls update_batch_status() with final counts, returns dict with keys: batch_id, new_rows, duplicate_rows, total_rows
- The ingest_to_raw() method must extract invoice_number, invoice_date, raw_supplier_name, base_amount from the post-mapping DataFrame (after ingest_file() runs) for storage in transactions_raw alongside the raw_data
- Existing method Ingestor.ingest_to_db() is not modified — signature and behaviour unchanged
- Verify: python -c "from src.ingestion.ingest import Ingestor; h = Ingestor.compute_source_row_hash({'a': 1, 'b': 2}); assert len(h) == 64; print('hash OK')"
- Verify: python -m pytest tests/test_ingest.py -v -- all existing tests pass

